//! VeriFe: prove a field of any post-Capella execution payload from one
//! EIP-4788 beacon block root.
//!
//! This ingot holds all of the proof logic and nothing else: no storage and no
//! I/O. It holds the anchor *interface* (`anchor::AnchorSource`) and both of
//! its implementations, but never decides which one a caller uses: that is the
//! one choice `contract` and `cli` each make for themselves. Those two are thin
//! shells over this ingot that differ only in where the anchor root and
//! SHA-256 come from.
//!
//! Module map (see `docs/architecture.md`):
//!
//! | Module     | Responsibility                                          |
//! | ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |
//! | `gindex`   | `const fn` generalized-index math: depth, concat, bounds |
//! | `layout`   | one Fe type per fork; proof shapes derived from it       |
//! | `hash`     | `ChunkHasher`: precompile 0x02 or software SHA-256       |
//! | `ssz`      | `uint64` chunk codec and the `List` length mix-in        |
//! | `merkle`   | branches, and vector and list elements, by gindex        |
//! | `header`   | `BeaconBlockHeader` hashing and field extraction         |
//! | `verify`   | the recent path and the historical path                  |
//! | `prove`    | the six steps composed, generic over the anchor source   |
//! | `anchor`   | `AnchorSource`: EIP-4788 on chain, a fixed root natively |
//! | `cache`    | the write-once rule for a stored period commitment       |
//! | `dispatch` | `Fork`, the boundary table, invariant 7 on proven slots |
